and to provide for the matters connected therewith or ancillary thereto.
It
is hereby enacted as follows--
CHAPTER-IV
AUTHORITIES OF THE UNIVERSITY
23. Senate.---(1) The Senate shall consist of--
(i) the Chancellor;
(ii) the Pro-Chancellor;
(iii) the Vice-Chancellor;
(iv) the Pro-Vice Chancellor, if appointed;
(v) the Members of the Syndicate;
(vi) the Deans;
(vii) the Director;
(viii) the Principals of
the constituent colleges;
(ix) the University Professors and Professors Emeritus;
(x) the Chairmen of the Teaching Departments;
(xi) the Officer or Teacher Incharge of
Student Affairs (by whatever designation called);
(xii) three Principals of affiliated colleges to be elected by the
Principals of all such colleges from amongst themselves;
(xiii) the Chairman Board
of Intermediate and Secondary Education located within the jurisdiction of the
University;
(xiv) the Chairman, Board
of Technical Education;
(xv) twelve University teachers having atleast
three years service to be elected by all University teachers;
(xvi) two registered
graduates to be elected by all such graduates from amongst themselves;
(xvii) three eminent
industrialists;
(xviii) one eminent
educationist;
(xix) one eminent research
scholar;
(xx) two persons from
amongst the eminent engineers and expert in engineering and technology;
(xxi) the Registrar;
(xxii) the Director of
Finance;
(xxiii) the Director
Planning and Development;
(xiv) the Controller of
Examination;
(xxv) the Resident
Auditor; and
(xxvi) the Librarian;
(2) The
Chancellor or in his absence, the Pro-Chancellor or in absence of both, the
Vice-Chancellor shall be the Chairman of the Senate.
(3) The
members of the Senate, other than ex-officio members shall hold office for
three years.
(4) The
Senate shall meet at least twice in every year on dates to be fixed by Vice Chancellor
with the consent of the Chancellor.
(5) The
quorum for meeting
of the Senate shall be one third of the total number of members, a fraction
being counted as one.
